# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 1: misdelivered), edited.

~ start
geneva_fairchild [afraid]: Oh, thank the moon you are strangers! I dropped three unsigned letters into the wrong cubbies, and if Miss Theodora sorts the dead-letter sack tonight, I shall die a second time.
geneva_fairchild [weary]: They were meant for Deputy Butterman. Now one sits on Constable Squire's desk, one went to the undertaker, and the square goat has the third. Please fetch them back.
* We will help -> accept
* Why not ask yourself? -> why
* Not now -> END

~ why
geneva_fairchild [afraid]: Constable Squire has eyes like carpentry nails, and Mr. Shade measures your collarbone whenever you say good evening. If I go near either of them, my knees will turn to suet.
-> start

~ accept
geneva_fairchild [smile]: Bless your boots! Look for lavender paper sealed with a crooked heart, and please do not read the bit about his ears.
quest misdelivered asked
set misdelivered_asked
-> END

~ doris_desk
Narrator: A square of lavender paper lies beside the constable's inkwell, smelling faintly of pressed violets and terror.
* [Sleight of Hand DC 12] Slip the letter away -> doris_ok | doris_caught
* Ask Doris for it plainly -> doris_ask
* Leave -> END

~ doris_ok
Narrator: {name} slides two fingers across the green blotter, and the lavender sheet vanishes into a coat pocket without a rustle.
set letter_doris
give geneva_letter_a
-> END

~ doris_caught
Narrator: A boot heel clicks on the floorboards right behind {name}'s shoulder.
doris_squire [neutral]: "Thine eyes are like two poached eggs in clouted cream." That is either a threat to the peace or poetry, and I lock up for both.
doris_squire [weary]: Keep the paper. I will sleep on whether to charge you, and you will sleep in the straw.
set letter_doris
give geneva_letter_a
jail wickermoor_constable_station:cells until days_since.jailed >= 1

~ doris_ask
doris_squire [neutral]: Take it. I read it twice to see if it was a cipher from the woods. It is badly spelled. I mean it kindly.
set letter_doris
give geneva_letter_a
-> END

~ mori_ask
Narrator: The undertaker's parlor smells of cedar shavings and damp wool. Mori opens a narrow drawer lined with velvet.
mori_shade [smile]: Unclaimed things come to me sooner or later, one way or another. I kept the lilac note in the third drawer, just in case.
* Ask for the letter -> mori_give
* [Persuasion DC 11] Tell him it matters to a girl -> mori_give | mori_fee
* Leave -> END

~ mori_give
mori_shade [smile]: Ah, the living and their little urgencies. Take it along, before the damp gets into the ink.
set letter_mori
give geneva_letter_b
-> END

~ mori_fee
mori_shade [sly]: Paper is light, but keeping secrets takes drawer space. Leave five coins for the ledger and give me a cousin's middle name for my list, and we are square.
gold -5
set letter_mori
give geneva_letter_b
-> END

~ goat
Narrator: The tether chain clinks against the founder's stone as the old billy goat works his jaw sideways. A corner of lavender paper sticks out from his beard.
* [Animal Handling DC 10] Coax the rest out -> goat_ok | goat_fail
* Leave -> END

~ goat_ok
Narrator: {name} scratches behind the goat's horned crown until his yellow eyes half-close, then draws the damp last third of the page from his teeth.
set letter_goat
give geneva_letter_c
-> END

~ goat_fail
Narrator: The billy goat fixes {name} with a flat yellow stare, gives one final chew, and swallows the last scrap with great dignity.
set letter_goat
-> END

~ deliver
geneva_fairchild [weary]: One from the desk, one from the parlor, and one mostly inside the goat. At least Miss Theodora will not pin them to the noticeboard.
geneva_fairchild [sad]: Only now I am looking at them, and my courage has gone cold. What on earth do I do about Howie?
* Tell Howie the truth yourself -> truth
* Let Howie think they were from Doris -> doris_lie
* [Deception DC 12] Forge a signature as 'a friend' -> forge_ok | forge_fail
* Burn the letters -> burn

~ truth
howie_butterman [smile]: For me? Well now, nobody ever compared my ears to buttercup petals before. I am not sure it is accurate, Miss Geneva, but I am mighty pleased.
set misdelivered_outcome = "truth"
quest misdelivered done
gold +20
standing cult +1
-> END

~ doris_lie
howie_butterman [smile]: Ma'am, I never knew you had such tender feelings under your truncheon.
doris_squire [angry]: Get back on your rounds, Butterman, before I fine you for loitering. And stand up straight.
set misdelivered_outcome = "lie"
quest misdelivered done
gold +10
-> END

~ forge_ok
Narrator: {name} matches the looping clerk-hand at the bottom of the page, signing it simply from a friend in the post office.
geneva_fairchild [smile]: That is neat enough to pass Miss Theodora herself. He will wonder next time he buys a stamp, and that is half the fun.
set misdelivered_outcome = "friend"
quest misdelivered done
gold +15
-> END

~ forge_fail
geneva_fairchild [weary]: Oh dear, the ink has blotted right through the paper. If I send that, he will think a spider died on the page.
-> deliver

~ burn
Narrator: The lavender scraps curl into black ash over the post office brazier, smelling briefly of cheap scent and sealing wax.
geneva_fairchild [smile]: There. Better ash than poached eggs in cream, honestly. Tomorrow I shall buy thick cream paper and write him something sensible.
set misdelivered_outcome = "burned"
quest misdelivered done
-> END
